      {
        "id": "p02",
        "title": "Report",
        "kind": "report",
        "body": "# The year, four ways\n\nNot one of these charts needs a library. Python works out every coordinate\nand writes the SVG, so what you see here is what the card shows \u2014 and it\nwould still draw on a laptop with no internet and nothing installed.\n\n## Who is ahead\n\n![[Bump: places over time|width=100%|radius=12]]\n\nA bump chart plots the *place*, not the score. Crossings are overtakes.\n\n## What moved between Q1 and Q4\n\n![[Slope: before and after|width=100%|radius=12]]\n\n## What the year is made of\n\nSquares you can count, rather than angles you cannot.\n\n![[Waffle: shares you can count|width=100%|radius=12]]\n\n## Where it came from\n\nEvery region gets the same square, so the colour is the only thing being\ncompared \u2014 on a real map the Highlands would shout and London would be a dot.\n\n![[Tile map: places, fairly|width=100%|radius=12]]\n"
      }
    ]
